Chaos Master <chaos@ig.com.br> wrote:
>Was playing a wizard (decided to take a break of barbarians. They became
>boring) when I missed one of the features that make spellcasters easy in
>ADOM:
>
>When you're low on power points, you can cast spells using your hit
>points (HP) as if they were power points. 
>
>This may seem "too good to be true" but there is a bad side effect - it
>abuses your stats. So the game balance is kept.
>
>Q: What do you think about implementing this in NetHack? I think it would
>not be >oo difficult to implement. Or is this too abusive?

With the rest of the game as it currently stands, this would be too
powerful.  Stat abuse is a non-penalty for anyone who's killed a unicorn.

Spellcasters are *supposed* to be harder to play than combat-wombats.
One of the nice things about Nethack is that unlike many roguelikes,
being a ludicrously tank-like warrior with minimal spellcasting ability
makes the game *easier*, not harder.

